  "provider": "anysearch",
  "tool": "extract",
  "content": "{\"url\":\"https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/\",\"title\":\"Mac Studio - Technical Specifications - Apple\",\"content\":\"# Mac Studio - Technical Specifications\\n\\nMac Studio, Model1\\n\\nMac Studio, Model2\\n\\nFinish\\n\\nSilver\\n\\nPrice\\n\\nChip\\n\\nApple M5 Max chip\\n- 18-core CPU with 6 super cores and 12 performance cores\\n- 32-core GPU\\n- Neural Accelerators\\n- Hardware-accelerated ray tracing\\n- 16-core Neural Engine\\n- 460GB/s memory bandwidth\\n\\nMedia Engine\\n- Hardware-accelerated H.264, HEVC, ProRes, and ProRes RAW\\n- Video decode engine\\n- Two video encode engines\\n- Two ProRes encode and decode engines\\n- AV1 decode\\n\\nConfigurable to:\\n- M5 Max with 18-core CPU, 40-core GPU, and 16-core Neural Engine (614GB/s memory bandwidth)\\n\\nApple M5 Ultra chip\\n- 30-core CPU with 10 super cores and 20 performance cores\\n- 64-core GPU\\n- Neural Accelerators\\n- Hardware-accelerated ray tracing\\n- 32-core Neural Engine\\n- 1.2TB/s memory bandwidth\\n\\nMedia Engine\\n- Hardware-accelerated H.264, HEVC, ProRes, and ProRes RAW\\n- Two video decode engines\\n- Four video encode engines\\n- Four ProRes encode and decode engines\\n- AV1 decode\\n\\nConfigurable to:\\n- M5 Ultra with 36-core CPU, 80-core GPU, and 32-core Neural Engine (1.2TB/s memory bandwidth)\\n\\nMemory\\n\\n36GB\\n- 36GB unified memory\\n\\nConfigurable to:\\n- 48GB, 64GB, or 128GB (M5 Max with 18-core CPU and 40-core GPU)\\n\\n96GB\\n- 96GB unified memory\\n\\nConfigurable to:\\n\\n256GB\\nor 512GB (M5 Ultra with 36-core CPU and 80-core GPU)\\n\\nStorage[1](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-1)\\n\\n512GB\\n- 512GB SSD\\n\\nConfigurable to:\\n- 1TB, 2TB, 4TB, or 8TB\\n\\n1TB\\n- 1TB SSD\\n\\nConfigurable to:\\n- 2TB, 4TB, 8TB, or 16TB\\n\\nDisplay Support\\n\\nM5 Max\\n\\nSupports up to five external displays over any combination of Thunderbolt and HDMI ports:\\n- Five displays: Four displays up to a native resolution of 6K at 60Hz or 4K at 165Hz, plus a fifth display with up to 5K at 60Hz over HDMI\\n- Up to three displays: Two displays up to a native resolution of 8K at 60Hz or 5K at 120Hz or 4K at 240Hz, plus a third display with up to 5K at 60Hz over HDMI\\n- Supports up to four external displays over a single Thunderbolt port\\n- Thunderbolt 5 (USB-C) ports support native DisplayPort 2.1 speeds\\n- Supports variable refresh rate (VRR), HDR, and multichannel audio\\n\\nM5 Ultra\\n\\nSupports up to eight external displays over any combination of Thunderbolt and HDMI ports:\\n- Eight displays up to a native resolution of 6K at 60Hz or 4K resolution at up to 165Hz\\n- Up to four displays up to a native resolution of 8K at 60Hz or 5K at 120Hz or 4K at 240Hz\\n- Supports up to four external displays over a single Thunderbolt port\\n- Thunderbolt 5 (USB-C) ports support native DisplayPort 2.1 speeds\\n- Supports variable refresh rate (VRR), HDR, and multichannel audio\\n\\n[Learn more about connecting a display to your Mac](https://support.apple.com/101910)\\n\\nAudio\\n\\n- Built-in speaker\\n- 3.5 mm headphone jack with advanced support for high-impedance headphones\\n- HDMI port supports multichannel audio output\\n\\nConnections and Expansion\\n\\nThunderbolt 5\\n\\n10Gb\\nEthernet\\n\\nUSB-A\\n\\nHDMI\\n2.1\\n\\n3.5 mm headphone jack\\n\\nFour Thunderbolt 5 (USB‑C) ports with support for:\\n- Thunderbolt 5 (up to 120Gb/s)\\n- USB 4 (up to 120Gb/s)\\n- USB 3 (up to 10Gb/s)\\n- DisplayPort 2.1\\n- Two USB 3 (USB‑A) ports (up to 5Gb/s)\\n- HDMI 2.1 port\\n- 10Gb Ethernet\\n- 3.5 mm headphone jack\\n\\nOn front (M5 Max):\\n- Two USB-C ports (up to 10Gb/s)\\n- SDXC card slot (UHS-II)\\n\\nOn front (M5 Ultra):\\n- Two Thunderbolt 5 ports (up to 120Gb/s)\\n- SDXC card slot (UHS-II)\\n\\nCommunications\\n\\nWireless\\n- Apple N1 wireless networking chip\\n- Wi‑Fi 7 (802.11be)[2](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-2)\\n- Bluetooth 6\\n- Thread networking technology\\n\\nEthernet\\n- 10Gb Ethernet (Nbase-T Ethernet with support for 1Gb, 2.5Gb, 5Gb, and 10Gb Ethernet using RJ-45 connector)\\n\\nSize and Weight\\n\\n- **Height:**3.7 inches (9.5 cm)\\n- **Width:**7.7 inches (19.7 cm)\\n- **Depth:**7.7 inches (19.7 cm)\\n- **Weight (M5 Max):**6.0 pounds (2.7 kg)[3](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-3)\\n- **Weight (M5 Ultra):**8.0 pounds (3.6 kg)[3](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-3)\\n\\nWidth:7.7 inches (19.7 cm)\\n\\nDepth:7.7 inches (19.7 cm)\\n\\nHeight:3.7 inches (9.5 cm)\\n\\nElectrical and Operating Requirements\\n\\n- **Line voltage:**100–240V AC\\n- **Frequency:**50Hz to 60Hz, single phase\\n- **Maximum continuous power:**480W\\n- **Operating temperature:**50° to 95° F (10° to 35° C)\\n- **Storage temperature:**–40° to 116° F (–40° to 47° C)\\n- **Relative humidity:**5% to 90% noncondensing\\n- **Operating altitude:**tested up to 16,400 feet (5000 meters)\\n\\nIn the Box\\n\\n- Mac Studio\\n- Power cord\\n\\nOperating System\\n\\nmacOS\\n\\nmacOS is the most advanced desktop operating system in the world. Siri AI is a powerful and capable assistant with personal context understanding, broad world knowledge, and onscreen awareness. Express yourself through photos and images, save time with Safari, and get more done with Apple Intelligence seamlessly integrated into your everyday apps and experiences. And iPhone Mirroring,[4](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-4)window tiling, Sidecar, and more help you stay productive.\\n\\nApple Intelligence[5](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-5)and Siri AI[6](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-6)\\n\\nThe next generation of Apple Intelligence is centered around you, integrated into your apps, and built with privacy. Apple Intelligence powers Siri AI — an entirely new version of Siri that’s more personal, conversational, and powerful, along with helpful features across apps.\\n\\n[Learn more](https://www.apple.com/apple-intelligence/)\\n\\nAccessibility\\n\\nAccessibility features help people with disabilities get the most out of their new Mac Studio. With built-in support for vision, hearing, mobility, and learning, you can create and do amazing things.\\n\\n[Learn more](https://www.apple.com/accessibility/features/?devices=mac)\\n\\nFeatures include:\\n\\n- VoiceOver\\n- Zoom\\n- Motion, display, and text settings\\n- Accessibility Reader\\n- Voice Control\\n- Switch Control\\n- Closed Captions\\n- Live Captions\\n- Personal Voice and Live Speech\\n\\nBuilt-in Apps[7](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-7)\\n\\nApp StoreBooksCalendarContactsFaceTimeFind MyFreeformGarageBandHomeiMovieiPhone MirroringKeynoteMailMapsMessagesMusicNewsNotesNumbersPagesPasswordsPhoto BoothPhotosPodcastsPreviewQuickTime PlayerRemindersSafariShortcutsStocksTime MachineTipsTVVoice MemosWeather\\n\\nConfigure to Order\\n\\nConfigure your Mac Studio with these options at[apple.com](https://www.apple.com/us/shop/goto/buy_mac/mac_studio):\\n\\n- M5 Max with 18-core CPU, 40-core GPU, and 16-core Neural Engine\\n- 48GB, 64GB, or 128GB unified memory (M5 Max with 18-core CPU and 40-core GPU)\\n- 1TB, 2TB, 4TB, or 8TB SSD\\n\\n- M5 Ultra with 36-core CPU, 80-core GPU, and 32-core Neural Engine\\n- 256GB unified memory\\n- 512GB unified memory (M5 Ultra with 36-core CPU and 80-core GPU)\\n- 2TB, 4TB, 8TB, or 16TB SSD\\n\\n## Mac Studio and the Environment\\n\\n[See the Mac Studio Product Environmental Report (PDF)](https://www.apple.com/environment/pdf/products/desktops/Mac_Studio_PER_Aug2026.pdf)\\n\\n### Progress toward Apple 2030\\n\\nApple 2030 is our goal to be carbon neutral across our value chain. We design our products to be less carbon intensive by prioritizing the use of recycled and renewable content and low-carbon materials while focusing on the energy efficiency of our software and hardware.[See Apple’s commitment](https://www.apple.com/environment/)\\n\\n### Materials\\n\\nMac Studio is made with 35% recycled content,[8](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-8)including:\\n- 100% recycled aluminum in the enclosure and thermal module sheet, chassis, and brackets\\n- 100% recycled copper in the thermal module pedestal and multiple printed circuit boards\\n- 100% recycled gold plating and tin solder in all Apple‑designed printed circuit boards\\n- 90% recycled steel in multiple thermal module components\\n\\n### Packaging\\n- 100% fiber-based packaging[9](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-9)\\n\\n### Energy\\n\\nENERGY STAR® certified[10](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-10)\\n\\n### Smarter chemistry[11](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-11)\\n\\nAll of the materials used in Apple products, accessories, and packaging are covered by the requirements of our[Regulated Substances Specification](https://www.apple.com/environment/pdf/Apple_Regulated_Substances_Specification.pdf), which was one of the first in industry to restrict the use of key substances of concern. See the latest[Environmental Progress Report](https://www.apple.com/environment/pdf/Apple_Environmental_Progress_Report_2026.pdf)to understand Apple’s recent efforts in phasing out these chemistries.\"}",
  "raw_content": "{\"url\":\"https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/\",\"title\":\"Mac Studio - Technical Specifications - Apple\",\"content\":\"# Mac Studio - Technical Specifications\\n\\nMac Studio, Model1\\n\\nMac Studio, Model2\\n\\nFinish\\n\\nSilver\\n\\nPrice\\n\\nChip\\n\\nApple M5 Max chip\\n- 18-core CPU with 6 super cores and 12 performance cores\\n- 32-core GPU\\n- Neural Accelerators\\n- Hardware-accelerated ray tracing\\n- 16-core Neural Engine\\n- 460GB/s memory bandwidth\\n\\nMedia Engine\\n- Hardware-accelerated H.264, HEVC, ProRes, and ProRes RAW\\n- Video decode engine\\n- Two video encode engines\\n- Two ProRes encode and decode engines\\n- AV1 decode\\n\\nConfigurable to:\\n- M5 Max with 18-core CPU, 40-core GPU, and 16-core Neural Engine (614GB/s memory bandwidth)\\n\\nApple M5 Ultra chip\\n- 30-core CPU with 10 super cores and 20 performance cores\\n- 64-core GPU\\n- Neural Accelerators\\n- Hardware-accelerated ray tracing\\n- 32-core Neural Engine\\n- 1.2TB/s memory bandwidth\\n\\nMedia Engine\\n- Hardware-accelerated H.264, HEVC, ProRes, and ProRes RAW\\n- Two video decode engines\\n- Four video encode engines\\n- Four ProRes encode and decode engines\\n- AV1 decode\\n\\nConfigurable to:\\n- M5 Ultra with 36-core CPU, 80-core GPU, and 32-core Neural Engine (1.2TB/s memory bandwidth)\\n\\nMemory\\n\\n36GB\\n- 36GB unified memory\\n\\nConfigurable to:\\n- 48GB, 64GB, or 128GB (M5 Max with 18-core CPU and 40-core GPU)\\n\\n96GB\\n- 96GB unified memory\\n\\nConfigurable to:\\n\\n256GB\\nor 512GB (M5 Ultra with 36-core CPU and 80-core GPU)\\n\\nStorage[1](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-1)\\n\\n512GB\\n- 512GB SSD\\n\\nConfigurable to:\\n- 1TB, 2TB, 4TB, or 8TB\\n\\n1TB\\n- 1TB SSD\\n\\nConfigurable to:\\n- 2TB, 4TB, 8TB, or 16TB\\n\\nDisplay Support\\n\\nM5 Max\\n\\nSupports up to five external displays over any combination of Thunderbolt and HDMI ports:\\n- Five displays: Four displays up to a native resolution of 6K at 60Hz or 4K at 165Hz, plus a fifth display with up to 5K at 60Hz over HDMI\\n- Up to three displays: Two displays up to a native resolution of 8K at 60Hz or 5K at 120Hz or 4K at 240Hz, plus a third display with up to 5K at 60Hz over HDMI\\n- Supports up to four external displays over a single Thunderbolt port\\n- Thunderbolt 5 (USB-C) ports support native DisplayPort 2.1 speeds\\n- Supports variable refresh rate (VRR), HDR, and multichannel audio\\n\\nM5 Ultra\\n\\nSupports up to eight external displays over any combination of Thunderbolt and HDMI ports:\\n- Eight displays up to a native resolution of 6K at 60Hz or 4K resolution at up to 165Hz\\n- Up to four displays up to a native resolution of 8K at 60Hz or 5K at 120Hz or 4K at 240Hz\\n- Supports up to four external displays over a single Thunderbolt port\\n- Thunderbolt 5 (USB-C) ports support native DisplayPort 2.1 speeds\\n- Supports variable refresh rate (VRR), HDR, and multichannel audio\\n\\n[Learn more about connecting a display to your Mac](https://support.apple.com/101910)\\n\\nAudio\\n\\n- Built-in speaker\\n- 3.5 mm headphone jack with advanced support for high-impedance headphones\\n- HDMI port supports multichannel audio output\\n\\nConnections and Expansion\\n\\nThunderbolt 5\\n\\n10Gb\\nEthernet\\n\\nUSB-A\\n\\nHDMI\\n2.1\\n\\n3.5 mm headphone jack\\n\\nFour Thunderbolt 5 (USB‑C) ports with support for:\\n- Thunderbolt 5 (up to 120Gb/s)\\n- USB 4 (up to 120Gb/s)\\n- USB 3 (up to 10Gb/s)\\n- DisplayPort 2.1\\n- Two USB 3 (USB‑A) ports (up to 5Gb/s)\\n- HDMI 2.1 port\\n- 10Gb Ethernet\\n- 3.5 mm headphone jack\\n\\nOn front (M5 Max):\\n- Two USB-C ports (up to 10Gb/s)\\n- SDXC card slot (UHS-II)\\n\\nOn front (M5 Ultra):\\n- Two Thunderbolt 5 ports (up to 120Gb/s)\\n- SDXC card slot (UHS-II)\\n\\nCommunications\\n\\nWireless\\n- Apple N1 wireless networking chip\\n- Wi‑Fi 7 (802.11be)[2](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-2)\\n- Bluetooth 6\\n- Thread networking technology\\n\\nEthernet\\n- 10Gb Ethernet (Nbase-T Ethernet with support for 1Gb, 2.5Gb, 5Gb, and 10Gb Ethernet using RJ-45 connector)\\n\\nSize and Weight\\n\\n- **Height:**3.7 inches (9.5 cm)\\n- **Width:**7.7 inches (19.7 cm)\\n- **Depth:**7.7 inches (19.7 cm)\\n- **Weight (M5 Max):**6.0 pounds (2.7 kg)[3](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-3)\\n- **Weight (M5 Ultra):**8.0 pounds (3.6 kg)[3](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-3)\\n\\nWidth:7.7 inches (19.7 cm)\\n\\nDepth:7.7 inches (19.7 cm)\\n\\nHeight:3.7 inches (9.5 cm)\\n\\nElectrical and Operating Requirements\\n\\n- **Line voltage:**100–240V AC\\n- **Frequency:**50Hz to 60Hz, single phase\\n- **Maximum continuous power:**480W\\n- **Operating temperature:**50° to 95° F (10° to 35° C)\\n- **Storage temperature:**–40° to 116° F (–40° to 47° C)\\n- **Relative humidity:**5% to 90% noncondensing\\n- **Operating altitude:**tested up to 16,400 feet (5000 meters)\\n\\nIn the Box\\n\\n- Mac Studio\\n- Power cord\\n\\nOperating System\\n\\nmacOS\\n\\nmacOS is the most advanced desktop operating system in the world. Siri AI is a powerful and capable assistant with personal context understanding, broad world knowledge, and onscreen awareness. Express yourself through photos and images, save time with Safari, and get more done with Apple Intelligence seamlessly integrated into your everyday apps and experiences. And iPhone Mirroring,[4](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-4)window tiling, Sidecar, and more help you stay productive.\\n\\nApple Intelligence[5](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-5)and Siri AI[6](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-6)\\n\\nThe next generation of Apple Intelligence is centered around you, integrated into your apps, and built with privacy. Apple Intelligence powers Siri AI — an entirely new version of Siri that’s more personal, conversational, and powerful, along with helpful features across apps.\\n\\n[Learn more](https://www.apple.com/apple-intelligence/)\\n\\nAccessibility\\n\\nAccessibility features help people with disabilities get the most out of their new Mac Studio. With built-in support for vision, hearing, mobility, and learning, you can create and do amazing things.\\n\\n[Learn more](https://www.apple.com/accessibility/features/?devices=mac)\\n\\nFeatures include:\\n\\n- VoiceOver\\n- Zoom\\n- Motion, display, and text settings\\n- Accessibility Reader\\n- Voice Control\\n- Switch Control\\n- Closed Captions\\n- Live Captions\\n- Personal Voice and Live Speech\\n\\nBuilt-in Apps[7](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-7)\\n\\nApp StoreBooksCalendarContactsFaceTimeFind MyFreeformGarageBandHomeiMovieiPhone MirroringKeynoteMailMapsMessagesMusicNewsNotesNumbersPagesPasswordsPhoto BoothPhotosPodcastsPreviewQuickTime PlayerRemindersSafariShortcutsStocksTime MachineTipsTVVoice MemosWeather\\n\\nConfigure to Order\\n\\nConfigure your Mac Studio with these options at[apple.com](https://www.apple.com/us/shop/goto/buy_mac/mac_studio):\\n\\n- M5 Max with 18-core CPU, 40-core GPU, and 16-core Neural Engine\\n- 48GB, 64GB, or 128GB unified memory (M5 Max with 18-core CPU and 40-core GPU)\\n- 1TB, 2TB, 4TB, or 8TB SSD\\n\\n- M5 Ultra with 36-core CPU, 80-core GPU, and 32-core Neural Engine\\n- 256GB unified memory\\n- 512GB unified memory (M5 Ultra with 36-core CPU and 80-core GPU)\\n- 2TB, 4TB, 8TB, or 16TB SSD\\n\\n## Mac Studio and the Environment\\n\\n[See the Mac Studio Product Environmental Report (PDF)](https://www.apple.com/environment/pdf/products/desktops/Mac_Studio_PER_Aug2026.pdf)\\n\\n### Progress toward Apple 2030\\n\\nApple 2030 is our goal to be carbon neutral across our value chain. We design our products to be less carbon intensive by prioritizing the use of recycled and renewable content and low-carbon materials while focusing on the energy efficiency of our software and hardware.[See Apple’s commitment](https://www.apple.com/environment/)\\n\\n### Materials\\n\\nMac Studio is made with 35% recycled content,[8](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-8)including:\\n- 100% recycled aluminum in the enclosure and thermal module sheet, chassis, and brackets\\n- 100% recycled copper in the thermal module pedestal and multiple printed circuit boards\\n- 100% recycled gold plating and tin solder in all Apple‑designed printed circuit boards\\n- 90% recycled steel in multiple thermal module components\\n\\n### Packaging\\n- 100% fiber-based packaging[9](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-9)\\n\\n### Energy\\n\\nENERGY STAR® certified[10](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-10)\\n\\n### Smarter chemistry[11](https://www.apple.com/mac-studio/specs/#footnote-11)\\n\\nAll of the materials used in Apple products, accessories, and packaging are covered by the requirements of our[Regulated Substances Specification](https://www.apple.com/environment/pdf/Apple_Regulated_Substances_Specification.pdf), which was one of the first in industry to restrict the use of key substances of concern. See the latest[Environmental Progress Report](https://www.apple.com/environment/pdf/Apple_Environmental_Progress_Report_2026.pdf)to understand Apple’s recent efforts in phasing out these chemistries.\"}",
